course: dictionary
lesson: 11701
title: Words for cause and credit
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Attributable is a formal word. It means something can be linked to a cause, so you can say where it comes from. «The rise in temperature is attributable to the sunny weather.» The sunny weather is the cause, and the rise came from it.
explain: The word is nearly always used with «to», as in «attributable to». Ask yourself: what caused this? If you can answer, the word fits. «The spill was attributable to a cracked jug.» A cracked jug caused the spill.
explain: Attributable can also mean that a saying or a piece of work came from a certain person. «The poem is attributable to Amara, who wrote it for the school magazine.» It means Amara wrote it. The word shows who made it, not what the poem is about.
fact: Attributable means that something can be caused by something, or can be said to come from someone.
fact: «Attributable to» is a common phrase: «The win was attributable to good teamwork.»
fact: Attributable is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in science, school reports and serious writing.
fact: To check the meaning, ask: what caused it, or who made it? If you can answer, attributable fits.
exercise: «The rise in temperature is attributable to the sunny weather.» What does attributable mean here? | Forgotten after | *Caused by | Painted in | Lost because of
exercise: «The poem is attributable to Amara.» What does this tell you? | The poem is about Amara's dog | Amara lost the poem | Amara is too young to read it | *Amara wrote the poem
exercise: «The spill was attributable to a cracked jug.» What is the cause of the spill? | A loud noise | A wet floor | *A cracked jug | A new cup
test: «Our win was attributable to good teamwork.» What was the cause of the win? | A lucky coin | Good weather | The referee's whistle | *Good teamwork
test: Which phrase is the best meaning of attributable? | Very loud | *Caused by, or come from | Bright and shiny | Given away for free
exam: «The mistake was attributable to tired eyes, not to carelessness.» Which best explains what attributable means here? | Carelessness was the only thing that was true | Tired eyes were blamed on the teacher | The mistake was never noticed | *The mistake was caused by tired eyes
